.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt AUTO-ROTATE-TOGGLE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm auto-rotate-toggle
.Nd toggle screen auto-rotation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
toggles the autorotate hold and shows the new state with
.Xr auto-rotate-osd 1 .
.Xr auto-rotate-osd 1
draws the glyph with
.Xr bosd 1 .
The usual chord is
.Sy Super+R .
Under KDE and Xfce the chord is
.Sy Super+O ,
because both bind
.Sy Super+R .
The plugin is offered at the greeter.
.Pp
A hold file means rotation is off.
.Nm
then runs
.Xr framework_autorotate 8
.Fl release
and shows the on glyph.
With no hold file,
.Nm
runs
.Fl hold
and shows the off glyph.
.Pp
The hold file is
.Pa ~/.framework_hold_autorotate
in the home directory from the password database for the real
user id.
When that lookup fails and the real user id is 0, the file is
.Pa /root/.framework_hold_autorotate .
.Ev HOME
is not used for root.
When the lookup fails for any other user, the directory is
.Ev HOME ,
or
.Pa /tmp .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "HOME"
.It Ev HOME
Fallback directory for the hold file when the password database
has no home for a non-root user.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.framework_hold_autorotate"
.It Pa ~/.framework_hold_autorotate
Hold file in the real user's home.
Present while auto-rotation is off.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the hold is toggled.
It exits 1 when given an argument.
A usage message is printed on standard error.
When
.Nm framework_autorotate
fails,
.Nm
exits with that status.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr auto-rotate-disable 1 ,
.Xr auto-rotate-enable 1 ,
.Xr auto-rotate-osd 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr framework_autorotate 8
